WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.570 --> 00:00:03.970
Trying

00:00:03.970 --> 00:00:06.473
to reassure each other and the world.

00:00:07.107 --> 00:00:09.409
America's top diplomat and China's leader

00:00:09.843 --> 00:00:11.144
were sitting down

00:00:11.144 --> 00:00:13.680
for talks earlier today, potentially

00:00:13.780 --> 00:00:15.782
a crucial step towards

00:00:15.782 --> 00:00:19.285
mending these US-China relations.

00:00:19.319 --> 00:00:20.086
The two

00:00:20.086 --> 00:00:21.121
global powers

00:00:21.121 --> 00:00:22.255
have been at odds,

00:00:22.255 --> 00:00:22.689
and that's,

00:00:22.689 --> 00:00:23.556
to put it

00:00:23.556 --> 00:00:25.892
mildly, over a host of issues

00:00:25.892 --> 00:00:27.060
that have sent relations,

00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:29.129
frankly, plunging to a new low

00:00:29.129 --> 00:00:30.497
Anthony Blinken,

00:00:30.497 --> 00:00:32.132
the first US secretary of state

00:00:32.132 --> 00:00:34.634
to visit Beijing in five years.

00:00:34.634 --> 00:00:35.602
Have a listen.

00:00:37.470 --> 00:00:38.304
Here in Beijing,

00:00:38.304 --> 00:00:40.140
I had an important conversation

00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:42.342
with President Xi Jinping,

00:00:42.375 --> 00:00:43.576
and I had candid,

00:00:43.576 --> 00:00:45.712
substantive and constructive discussions

00:00:45.712 --> 00:00:46.980
with my counterparts

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:48.248
director Wang Yi

00:00:48.248 --> 00:00:50.617
and State Councilor Chen Gong.

00:00:50.617 --> 00:00:52.052
I appreciate the hospitality

00:00:52.052 --> 00:00:54.554
extended by our hosts

00:00:54.721 --> 00:00:56.289
in every meeting

00:00:56.322 --> 00:00:58.558
I stress that direct engagement

00:00:58.658 --> 00:00:59.759
and sustained communication

00:00:59.759 --> 00:01:00.927
at senior levels

00:01:00.927 --> 00:01:01.761
is the best way

00:01:01.761 --> 00:01:03.696
to responsibly manage our differences

00:01:03.696 --> 00:01:04.531
and ensure

00:01:04.531 --> 00:01:05.365
that competition

00:01:05.365 --> 00:01:07.600
does not veer into conflict.

00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:08.635
And I heard the same

00:01:08.635 --> 00:01:10.637
from my Chinese counterparts.

00:01:10.637 --> 00:01:12.338
We both agree on the need

00:01:12.338 --> 00:01:13.740
to stabilize our relationship

00:01:15.608 --> 00:01:16.142
Well, for

00:01:16.142 --> 00:01:17.310
his part, President

00:01:17.310 --> 00:01:20.280
Xi says there are reasons to be hopeful.

00:01:20.313 --> 00:01:21.314
Have a listen.

00:01:23.016 --> 00:01:24.684
To financial planning.

00:01:24.684 --> 00:01:26.019
The Chinese side has made

00:01:26.019 --> 00:01:27.353
our position clear,

00:01:27.353 --> 00:01:28.221
and the two sides

00:01:28.221 --> 00:01:29.589
have agreed to follow

00:01:29.589 --> 00:01:31.291
through the common understandings.

00:01:31.291 --> 00:01:32.258
President Biden

00:01:32.258 --> 00:01:34.727
and I had reached in Bali.

00:01:34.727 --> 00:01:36.963
The two sides have also made progress

00:01:36.963 --> 00:01:38.298
and reached agreement

00:01:38.298 --> 00:01:40.400
on some specific issues.

00:01:40.400 --> 00:01:42.001
This is very good

00:01:43.169 --> 00:01:44.838
Well, key points of contention

00:01:44.838 --> 00:01:46.206
between the two global

00:01:46.206 --> 00:01:49.809
superpowers of Taiwan, spying

00:01:49.943 --> 00:01:51.244
and the war in Ukraine.

00:01:51.244 --> 00:01:51.578
And don't

00:01:51.578 --> 00:01:52.879
forget us restrictions

00:01:52.879 --> 00:01:55.782
on the sale of semiconductor chips.

00:01:55.815 --> 00:01:56.883
CNN's U.S.

00:01:56.883 --> 00:01:58.451
security correspondent

00:01:58.451 --> 00:01:59.686
Kelly Atwood has been

00:01:59.686 --> 00:02:01.254
reporting from Beijing.

00:02:01.254 --> 00:02:01.654
And here's

00:02:01.654 --> 00:02:02.155
what she

00:02:02.155 --> 00:02:04.224
told my colleagues a little bit earlier.

00:02:06.059 --> 00:02:07.293
One of the things that the

00:02:07.293 --> 00:02:08.261
secretary of state

00:02:08.261 --> 00:02:10.530
set out here in Beijing to accomplish

00:02:10.797 --> 00:02:12.432
was reestablish pushing,

00:02:12.432 --> 00:02:13.299
setting up

00:02:13.299 --> 00:02:15.301
military to military channels

00:02:15.301 --> 00:02:16.703
of communication,

00:02:16.703 --> 00:02:18.771
essentially lines of communication

00:02:18.771 --> 00:02:19.939
that could be used

00:02:19.939 --> 00:02:21.541
in the case of a crisis

00:02:21.541 --> 00:02:23.042
between the two countries.

00:02:23.042 --> 00:02:24.010
That's given

00:02:24.010 --> 00:02:25.111
the fact that there have been

00:02:25.111 --> 00:02:25.778
two recent

00:02:25.778 --> 00:02:27.147
military incidents

00:02:27.147 --> 00:02:29.015
between the US and China

00:02:29.015 --> 00:02:30.216
just in recent weeks

00:02:30.216 --> 00:02:31.050
in the South China

00:02:31.050 --> 00:02:33.086
Sea in the air and by

00:02:33.086 --> 00:02:34.921
and by the sea as well.

00:02:34.921 --> 00:02:36.623
But that is not an area

00:02:36.623 --> 00:02:38.491
where he is headed back to Washington

00:02:38.491 --> 00:02:39.192
with a victory.

00:02:39.192 --> 00:02:40.760
He said that the Chinese didn't agree

00:02:40.760 --> 00:02:42.061
to set up those channels.

00:02:42.061 --> 00:02:43.563
Listen to what he told me earlier

00:02:43.563 --> 00:02:44.931
today at the press conference.

00:02:47.433 --> 00:02:48.468
This is also something

00:02:48.468 --> 00:02:51.004
that I raised repeatedly

00:02:51.604 --> 00:02:52.238
during this trip.

00:02:52.238 --> 00:02:53.139
I think

00:02:53.139 --> 00:02:54.174
it's absolutely vital

00:02:54.174 --> 00:02:56.709
that we have these kind of communications

00:02:56.709 --> 00:02:58.711
military to military.

00:02:59.045 --> 00:03:01.648
That imperative, I think, was only

00:03:02.682 --> 00:03:05.518
underscored by recent incidents

00:03:05.518 --> 00:03:07.854
that we saw in the air and on the seas.

00:03:09.022 --> 00:03:10.223
And

00:03:10.757 --> 00:03:12.125
at this moment,

00:03:12.392 --> 00:03:13.560
China has not agreed to move

00:03:13.560 --> 00:03:14.761
forward with that.

00:03:15.595 --> 00:03:16.729
I think that's an issue

00:03:16.729 --> 00:03:18.831
that we have to keep working on.

00:03:18.831 --> 00:03:21.668
It is very important that we restore

00:03:21.668 --> 00:03:22.936
those channels

00:03:26.472 --> 00:03:27.373
Now, we also know

00:03:27.373 --> 00:03:28.141
one of the issues

00:03:28.141 --> 00:03:29.442
that you mentioned out of the gates

00:03:29.442 --> 00:03:31.411
there was Taiwan.

00:03:31.411 --> 00:03:32.378
One of the readouts

00:03:32.378 --> 00:03:33.213
from a meeting

00:03:33.213 --> 00:03:35.181
that the secretary had here made clear

00:03:35.181 --> 00:03:36.683
that Chinese officials

00:03:36.683 --> 00:03:39.118
made demands when it comes to Taiwan.

00:03:39.285 --> 00:03:39.686
They said

00:03:39.686 --> 00:03:40.486
that is the area

00:03:40.486 --> 00:03:42.689
that presents the most pronounced risk

00:03:42.922 --> 00:03:44.757
to us. China relations.

00:03:44.757 --> 00:03:46.259
The secretary of state said

00:03:46.259 --> 00:03:47.560
at the press conference

00:03:47.560 --> 00:03:48.895
that he made clear

00:03:48.895 --> 00:03:51.064
that the US has concerns about China's

00:03:51.264 --> 00:03:53.166
provocative actions

00:03:53.166 --> 00:03:55.235
when it comes to Taiwan.

00:03:55.235 --> 00:03:57.337
And the United States doesn't right now

00:03:57.337 --> 00:03:59.405
support Taiwan's independence,

00:03:59.639 --> 00:04:01.474
but they don't support either

00:04:01.474 --> 00:04:03.576
side taking unilateral actions

00:04:03.576 --> 00:04:05.378
that could upend the status

00:04:05.378 --> 00:04:06.179
quo currently.

00:04:06.179 --> 00:04:08.348
Now, there was progress forward movement

00:04:08.581 --> 00:04:09.515
on another topic,

00:04:09.515 --> 00:04:11.651
and that's an issue of synthetic opioids,

00:04:11.651 --> 00:04:13.419
which of course is a major killer

00:04:13.419 --> 00:04:15.121
of Americans back home

00:04:15.121 --> 00:04:16.856
setting all the precursor chemicals

00:04:16.856 --> 00:04:19.025
or fentanyl largely come from China.

00:04:19.025 --> 00:04:20.159
Secretary of State said

00:04:20.159 --> 00:04:22.428
that the two sides agreed to stand up

00:04:22.662 --> 00:04:23.997
a working level

00:04:23.997 --> 00:04:25.365
meeting on this,

00:04:25.365 --> 00:04:27.133
a group that can actually address

00:04:27.133 --> 00:04:28.501
this issue to stem

00:04:28.501 --> 00:04:30.270
that flow of those chemicals

00:04:30.270 --> 00:04:32.305
into the United States and on Ukraine.

00:04:32.472 --> 00:04:34.240
They also addressed the war in Ukraine.

00:04:34.240 --> 00:04:35.108
The secretary said

00:04:35.108 --> 00:04:36.776
that Chinese officials once again said

00:04:36.776 --> 00:04:38.878
that they are not going to be sending

00:04:38.878 --> 00:04:40.013
lethal aid

00:04:40.013 --> 00:04:41.648
to Russia to be used in that war,

00:04:41.648 --> 00:04:42.482
but they're still watching

00:04:42.482 --> 00:04:44.584
Chinese companies incredibly closely

00:04:46.786 --> 00:04:47.654
Well, that was CNN's

00:04:47.654 --> 00:04:49.656
Connie Atwood reporting from Beijing.

00:04:49.689 --> 00:04:51.224
I want to bring in my colleague

00:04:51.224 --> 00:04:53.793
and current live from Hong Kong.

00:04:53.793 --> 00:04:57.330
And I think what we are hearing

00:04:57.964 --> 00:04:58.831
out of

00:04:58.831 --> 00:05:02.101
Beijing today is absolutely fascinating.

00:05:02.402 --> 00:05:03.303
Just pick apart

00:05:03.303 --> 00:05:06.172
what we know at this point and why

00:05:06.306 --> 00:05:09.075
it is potentially so significant.

00:05:10.810 --> 00:05:13.413
Well, certainly on the issue

00:05:13.413 --> 00:05:15.014
of of trade, I mean, these

00:05:15.014 --> 00:05:18.017
these are two countries Becky, that,

00:05:18.051 --> 00:05:18.451
you know,

00:05:18.451 --> 00:05:21.254
the largest economies in the world,

00:05:21.254 --> 00:05:24.190
the top two trading partners,

00:05:25.258 --> 00:05:27.593
almost $700 billion worth of trade goes

00:05:27.593 --> 00:05:31.097
between the United States and China.

00:05:31.097 --> 00:05:33.299
And we know that China,

00:05:33.299 --> 00:05:33.666
you know,

00:05:33.666 --> 00:05:36.569
it needs the United States, its postcode

00:05:36.703 --> 00:05:40.473
recovery has not been as strong as it had

00:05:40.473 --> 00:05:40.940
hoped.

00:05:40.940 --> 00:05:42.208
We know that U.S.

00:05:42.208 --> 00:05:44.610
unemployment is is soaring there.

00:05:44.610 --> 00:05:46.412
The property market is

00:05:46.412 --> 00:05:48.981
is incredibly sluggish.

00:05:48.981 --> 00:05:51.617
And China needs its US export

00:05:52.051 --> 00:05:54.220
market to flourish.

00:05:54.220 --> 00:05:57.657
The US makes up 16% of Chinese exports.

00:05:57.657 --> 00:06:01.828
So that is why this is so important.

00:06:01.861 --> 00:06:05.365
It is hoped that that from this

00:06:05.598 --> 00:06:07.500
visit is a two day visit,

00:06:07.500 --> 00:06:08.468
which we didn't know

00:06:08.468 --> 00:06:10.503
if Blinken was going to meet with XI.

00:06:10.503 --> 00:06:11.137
You know, that

00:06:11.137 --> 00:06:12.638
came at the very last minute,

00:06:12.638 --> 00:06:14.140
obviously off the back of

00:06:14.140 --> 00:06:15.808
10 hours worth of

00:06:15.808 --> 00:06:17.777
of accumulative meetings

00:06:17.777 --> 00:06:18.811
with the Foreign Ministry

00:06:18.811 --> 00:06:21.214
and then China's top diplomat today.

00:06:21.981 --> 00:06:24.884
But but, you know, because of that,

00:06:25.385 --> 00:06:27.954
Blinken met with XI.

00:06:27.954 --> 00:06:29.789
Now, Becky, a short time ago,

00:06:29.789 --> 00:06:31.190
we heard from the Ministry

00:06:31.190 --> 00:06:31.958
of Foreign Affairs.

00:06:31.958 --> 00:06:33.292
They held a briefing

00:06:33.292 --> 00:06:35.795
with reporters in Beijing after

00:06:36.062 --> 00:06:38.164
Blinken departed for London.

00:06:38.865 --> 00:06:40.099
It was Yang Tao.

00:06:40.099 --> 00:06:41.033
He's the director

00:06:41.033 --> 00:06:42.468
general of the ministry's

00:06:42.468 --> 00:06:43.669
North American Ocean

00:06:43.669 --> 00:06:46.105
and Oceanian Affairs Department.

00:06:46.105 --> 00:06:47.340
And he said

00:06:47.340 --> 00:06:50.042
that this visit by Blinken marks

00:06:50.042 --> 00:06:53.613
a new beginning in bilateral relations,

00:06:53.613 --> 00:06:55.748
which obviously is is very conciliatory.

00:06:55.815 --> 00:06:56.949
It's very hopeful.

00:06:56.949 --> 00:06:58.251
It's very positive language

00:06:58.251 --> 00:06:59.552
coming out of Beijing.

00:06:59.552 --> 00:07:01.654
He did, however, say, Becky,

00:07:01.654 --> 00:07:02.688
that he rejects

00:07:02.688 --> 00:07:04.257
Washington's strategy

00:07:04.257 --> 00:07:06.259
of derisking from China.

00:07:06.259 --> 00:07:08.194
And that is something that we heard

00:07:08.194 --> 00:07:10.263
from Anthony Blinken.

00:07:10.296 --> 00:07:11.130
He went on to say that

00:07:11.130 --> 00:07:13.966
this us us simply repackaging,

00:07:14.700 --> 00:07:17.437
decoupling, as de-risking from China.

00:07:17.670 --> 00:07:19.906
The policy is turning away from stability

00:07:19.906 --> 00:07:20.940
and opportunity.

00:07:20.940 --> 00:07:23.009
It won't solve US problems.

00:07:23.342 --> 00:07:25.645
It will cause more problems.

00:07:25.878 --> 00:07:26.579
Globally.

00:07:26.579 --> 00:07:29.415
Now, obviously, Becky, the hope is that,

00:07:29.649 --> 00:07:30.216
you know,

00:07:30.216 --> 00:07:31.250
communication lines

00:07:31.250 --> 00:07:32.452
have been reestablished.

00:07:32.452 --> 00:07:34.120
That was always the aim.

00:07:34.120 --> 00:07:35.855
And that from this

00:07:35.855 --> 00:07:36.756
the treasury secretary

00:07:36.756 --> 00:07:37.857
from the United States, the commerce

00:07:37.857 --> 00:07:38.958
secretary from the United States,

00:07:38.958 --> 00:07:41.027
will now come to visit

00:07:41.027 --> 00:07:43.129
Beijing in the coming weeks because

00:07:45.198 --> 00:07:45.598
let's just

00:07:45.598 --> 00:07:45.965
be quite

00:07:45.965 --> 00:07:49.469
clear about the definition of de-risking.

00:07:49.502 --> 00:07:50.036
Thank you all,

00:07:50.036 --> 00:07:51.871
because I think it's important here.

00:07:51.871 --> 00:07:53.906
And you you will hear

00:07:54.707 --> 00:07:56.142
a lot of countries

00:07:56.142 --> 00:07:57.710
talking about de-risking at the moment.

00:07:57.710 --> 00:07:59.011
What it means is the

00:07:59.011 --> 00:08:00.446
and he is a strict

00:08:00.446 --> 00:08:01.981
definition of this phenomenon

00:08:01.981 --> 00:08:03.783
of financial institutions,

00:08:03.783 --> 00:08:05.084
country terminating

00:08:05.084 --> 00:08:06.219
or restricting business

00:08:06.219 --> 00:08:07.687
relationships with clients

00:08:07.687 --> 00:08:08.888
or categories of clients

00:08:08.888 --> 00:08:12.158
to avoid rather than manage risk.

00:08:12.158 --> 00:08:12.892
It it

00:08:12.892 --> 00:08:13.993
tends to be used

00:08:13.993 --> 00:08:14.961
within the context

00:08:14.961 --> 00:08:17.063
of financial institutions.

00:08:17.063 --> 00:08:18.331
And that's where you would hear it.

00:08:18.331 --> 00:08:18.631
If you're

00:08:18.631 --> 00:08:19.799
across your business news,

00:08:19.799 --> 00:08:21.000
you'd have heard the term

00:08:21.000 --> 00:08:22.635
derisking in the past.

00:08:22.635 --> 00:08:24.770
It's so interesting to see

00:08:24.770 --> 00:08:27.206
global leaders using the term we heard

00:08:27.206 --> 00:08:28.808
it used at G7 of late.

00:08:28.808 --> 00:08:29.575
We've heard

00:08:29.575 --> 00:08:30.543
it use once again

00:08:30.543 --> 00:08:32.612
by the Americans here in Beijing.

00:08:32.612 --> 00:08:34.247
It is a term that you should become

00:08:34.247 --> 00:08:35.848
more familiar with.

